	Prosody Framer 
secname sort

	Create a Framer 
apifn	sm_framer_create
params	sm_framer_create_parms createp
	The created framer.
field	tSMFramerId framer out
	A value obtained from
fnref   sm_open_module
	which indicates the module on which the framer is to be created.
field   tSMModuleId module in
unstruct
	Creates a Framer .
explain
	0
retval
error   ERR_SM_DEVERR - device error
error   ERR_SM_NO_RESOURCES - if no suitable output channel free
error   ERR_SM_NO_SUCH_MODULE - if invalid module identifier specified

	Destroy a Framer 
apifn	sm_framer_destroy
	The Framer to destroy. Must have been previously created by a call to
fnref	sm_framer_create
	.
param	tSMFramerId framer
	Destroys a Framer.
explain
	0
retval
error   ERR_SM_DEVERR - device error

	Connect a datafeed to an input of a Framer .
apifn	sm_framer_datafeed_connect
params	sm_framer_datafeed_connect_parms datafeedp
	The datafeed object to be connected. 
field	tSMDatafeedId data_source in
	The framer to connect the datafeed to.
field	tSMFramerId framer in
	The input to which the datafeed is to be connected.
	If direction is 0, then the enframer-side input is connected.
	If direction is 1, then the deframer-side input is connected.
field	tSM_INT direction in
unstruct
	Connect a datafeed to one of the inputs of the Framer. 
explain
	0
retval
error   ERR_SM_DEVERR - device error
error   ERR_SM_NO_RESOURCES - direction was given an illegal value

	Disconnect a datafeed from a Framer.
apifn	sm_framer_datafeed_disconnect
params	sm_framer_datafeed_disconnect_parms datafeedp
	The framer to disconnect the datafeed from.
field	tSMFramerId framer in
	The input of the framer to be disconnected.
	If direction is 0, then the enframer-side input is disconnected.
	If direction is 1, then the deframer-side input is disconnected.
field   tSM_INT direction in
unstruct
	Disconnect a datafeed on one of the inputs of the Framer.
explain
	0
retval
error   ERR_SM_DEVERR - device error

	Get an event object for the Framer 
apifn	sm_framer_get_event
params	sm_framer_event_parms eventp
	The framer.
field	tSMFramerId framer in
	The event identifier.
field	tSMEventId event out
unstruct
	Returns an event object for the framer that can be waited on using 
fnref	smd_ev_wait
	.
	The event will be signalled when a status change occurs on the framer.
explain
	0
retval
error	ERR_SM_DEVERR - device error

	Fetch status info on Framer 
apifn	sm_framer_status
params	sm_framer_status_parms statusp
	The Framer.
field	tSMFramerId framer in
	The status.
enumstart kSMFramerStatus
	The framer is running
enum	kSMFramerStatusRunning
	The framer is not running
enum	kSMFramerStatusStopped
	The framer has changed state
enum	kSMFramerStatusNewState
enumend status out
	The new state of the framer. Only valid when the status field is kSMFramerStatusNewState.
	If new_state is 0, then the framer is now out of sync.
	If new_state is 1, then the framer is now in sync.
field	tSM_INT new_state out
unstruct
	Returns the status of the Framer.
explain
	0
retval
error   ERR_SM_DEVERR - device error

	Get datafeed from Framer.
apifn	sm_framer_get_datafeed
params	sm_framer_datafeed_parms datafeedp
	The framer from which to obtain a datafeed.
field	tSMFramerId framer in
	The direction of datafeed to fetch. If direction is 0, then the enframer-side datafeed is fetched. If direction is 1, then the deframer-side datafeed is fetched.
field	tSM_INT direction in
	The datafeed object associated with the Framer .
field	tSMDatafeedId datafeed out
unstruct
	Request a datafeed identifier from a Framer .
	This identifier can subsequently used in a call such as
fnref	sm_tdmtx_datafeed_connect
	or
fnref	sm_channel_datafeed_connect.
explain
	0
retval
error   ERR_SM_DEVERR - device error
